%Hence its leftmost column corresponds to $L+1$ time steps back and the rightmost column corresponds to 0 time steps back.  The goal is to skew this matrix into one that is absolute-by-absolute with rows indexed by queries, columns by keys.  
%This procedure assumes the starting matrix is lower triangular, such as in self-attention, and 
%The ``skewing'' procedure is as follows, illustrated in Figure~\ref{fig:skew}:
%\begin{enumerate}
%   \item Pad a dummy column vector of length $L$ before the leftmost column (Figure~\ref{fig:skew} middle panel).
%   \item Reshape the matrix to have shape $(L+1, L)$ (Figure~\ref{fig:skew} right panel).
